59
00:05:02,920 --> 00:05:03,800
Tastes better with every sip.

60
00:05:04,680 --> 00:05:05,040
Really?

61
00:05:06,480 --> 00:05:08,319
I'll get you some Dahongpao another time.

62
00:05:09,680 --> 00:05:10,439
No need, no need.

63
00:05:11,639 --> 00:05:11,959
Okay.

64
00:05:12,480 --> 00:05:13,199
Okay, thanks.

65
00:05:15,439 --> 00:05:17,439
Director Zhao, you've got lint on your back too.

66
00:05:20,920 --> 00:05:21,759
What time is the meeting?

67
00:05:24,600 --> 00:05:25,240
In five minutes.

68
00:05:28,160 --> 00:05:28,439
Alright.

69
00:05:29,439 --> 00:05:29,839
All done.

70
00:05:30,319 --> 00:05:31,040
Thanks, thanks.

71
00:05:36,759 --> 00:05:37,319
Look at this.

72
00:05:38,560 --> 00:05:39,360
This is already the second steep.

73
00:05:40,079 --> 00:05:41,120
Look at the color. Just look.

74
00:05:43,000 --> 00:05:43,639
I've been drinking this.

75
00:05:43,800 --> 00:05:45,040
Let me pour you a cup.

76
00:05:45,199 --> 00:05:45,519
Sure.

77
00:05:45,519 --> 00:05:46,319
Here, here.

78
00:05:46,800 --> 00:05:47,319
We still have time.

79
00:05:49,120 --> 00:05:50,079
I've always believed...

80
00:05:50,920 --> 00:05:52,040
that this publicity work...

81
00:05:52,800 --> 00:05:54,519
is definitely not just about shouting slogans.

82
00:05:55,240 --> 00:05:57,639
Therefore, our Publicity Department's top priority...

83
00:05:58,199 --> 00:06:00,240
is to organize and guide

84
00:06:00,879 --> 00:06:02,199
all public security organs in the city

85
00:06:03,199 --> 00:06:04,240
regarding their public outreach

86
00:06:04,800 --> 00:06:07,240
and public opinion guidance,

87
00:06:07,519 --> 00:06:08,920
ensuring accuracy and standardization.

88
00:06:10,439 --> 00:06:11,319
Because it concerns...

89
00:06:11,959 --> 00:06:12,839
our public security system's...

90
00:06:13,800 --> 00:06:15,240
overall public image.

91
00:06:17,279 --> 00:06:19,839
The Bureau Party Committee has decided...

92
00:06:27,639 --> 00:06:28,800
that Comrade Zhao Guohua...

93
00:06:29,240 --> 00:06:30,439
will serve as the Publicity Department's...

94
00:06:31,240 --> 00:06:31,720
Director.

95
00:06:42,560 --> 00:06:43,480
Comrade Zhao Guohua

96
00:06:44,160 --> 00:06:44,920
is modest and amiable,

97
00:06:45,560 --> 00:06:46,519
and works proactively and diligently.

98
00:06:47,319 --> 00:06:48,639
In his past work,

99
00:06:49,759 --> 00:06:51,879
his achievements have been noteworthy.

100
00:06:52,839 --> 00:06:55,240
I hope that in future publicity work,

101
00:06:56,000 --> 00:06:56,720
he will lead our comrades

102
00:06:57,720 --> 00:06:59,920
to be transparent and focus on practical results,

103
00:07:00,560 --> 00:07:01,199
and keep up the good work.

104
00:07:03,680 --> 00:07:04,040
Understood.

105
00:07:06,480 --> 00:07:07,040
In addition,

106
00:07:08,040 --> 00:07:08,720
the Bureau Party Committee

107
00:07:08,920 --> 00:07:09,959
has also discussed our

108
00:07:09,959 --> 00:07:10,759
SWAT detachment's

109
00:07:11,160 --> 00:07:12,040
Political Commissar candidate,

110
00:07:13,920 --> 00:07:15,680
and decided that Comrade Tan Yan

111
00:07:17,040 --> 00:07:19,519
will be assigned to the SWAT detachment as Political Commissar

112
00:07:20,000 --> 00:07:20,759
for a period of two years.

113
00:07:59,360 --> 00:07:59,639
No, seriously.

114
00:08:00,040 --> 00:08:02,279
Why did he appoint Lao Zhao as director?

115
00:08:03,959 --> 00:08:06,160
Yeah. Did you offend him somehow?

116
00:08:08,600 --> 00:08:10,600
I'm telling you, this just isn't right.

117
00:08:11,240 --> 00:08:12,600
When it comes to his work, Lao Tan...

118
00:08:12,600 --> 00:08:13,839
...has always been incredibly dedicated.

119
00:08:34,279 --> 00:08:35,679
I think it's good you're going to SWAT.

120
00:08:42,720 --> 00:08:44,720
What's so great about the SWAT team?

121
00:08:46,440 --> 00:08:48,159
Sleeping in a car hugging a rifle.

122
00:08:49,120 --> 00:08:51,200
It's either training or patrolling.

123
00:08:51,440 --> 00:08:53,960
You barely get any real cases all year.

124
00:08:55,039 --> 00:08:57,080
Going there is just a waste of time.

125
00:09:00,480 --> 00:09:01,039
Well, our local precinct

126
00:09:01,039 --> 00:09:02,720
barely gets any real cases all year either.

127
00:09:04,039 --> 00:09:05,279
So we're just wasting time too?

128
00:09:27,480 --> 00:09:28,159
Stop fighting it.

129
00:09:45,360 --> 00:09:46,159
I have to fight it.

130
00:10:25,600 --> 00:10:26,759
Stop giving me a hard time.

131
00:10:27,120 --> 00:10:28,320
Sure, they dropped the "Deputy" title,

132
00:10:28,720 --> 00:10:30,000
but everyone knows it's a dead-end job.

133
00:10:30,639 --> 00:10:32,039
I remember you have a classmate

134
00:10:32,440 --> 00:10:33,360
in the Municipal Organization Department.

135
00:10:33,639 --> 00:10:34,440
Director Xie, hello.

136
00:10:34,440 --> 00:10:35,960
This is Xiao Tan, from the Municipal Bureau.

137
00:10:36,559 --> 00:10:37,279
Tan Yan. Tan Yan.

138
00:10:39,960 --> 00:10:41,960
I actually have a favor to ask you.

139
00:10:42,840 --> 00:10:44,000
You retired last month?

140
00:10:45,080 --> 00:10:45,639
Director Xie...

141
00:10:46,200 --> 00:10:47,840
I wish you good health and a happy retirement!

142
00:10:48,279 --> 00:10:49,720
I'll visit you when I have time!

143
00:10:50,519 --> 00:10:51,559
Goodbye, goodbye, goodbye.

144
00:10:59,559 --> 00:11:01,960
You have a high school classmate whose dad is in the Municipal Committee,

145
00:11:05,840 --> 00:11:06,720
working in logistics.

146
00:11:07,120 --> 00:11:08,200
He won't be able to help with this.

147
00:11:12,039 --> 00:11:14,080
If you really don't want to go,

148
00:11:14,080 --> 00:11:15,279
just tell Director Guo directly.

149
00:11:16,519 --> 00:11:17,559
Asking anyone else for help

150
00:11:17,559 --> 00:11:18,519
will just be a bother.

151
00:11:19,480 --> 00:11:20,799
I'll definitely have to talk to him,

152
00:11:22,960 --> 00:11:24,960
but I need to figure out what to say.

153
00:11:28,279 --> 00:11:30,679
This decision was made by the Bureau Party Committee.

154
00:11:31,919 --> 00:11:33,039
I can't just give an excuse

155
00:11:33,519 --> 00:11:34,720
that makes it sound like

156
00:11:34,720 --> 00:11:35,960
it's for personal reasons.

157
00:11:36,559 --> 00:11:37,559
That won't work.

158
00:11:44,960 --> 00:11:46,080
Train the body!

159
00:11:46,360 --> 00:11:49,120
Train the body, keep a steady mind!

160
00:11:49,279 --> 00:11:52,080
Build your muscles, ready for a beating!

161
00:11:52,799 --> 00:11:53,279
One, two, one, two!

162
00:11:53,279 --> 00:11:54,600
Isn't that our new commissar?

163
00:11:55,039 --> 00:11:55,919
One, two, one!

164
00:11:55,919 --> 00:11:57,360
I thought he wasn't starting until next week?

165
00:11:57,879 --> 00:12:00,360
Probably just checking out the work environment first.

166
00:12:00,720 --> 00:12:02,519
Maybe he'll change his mind if it looks too shabby.

167
00:12:02,879 --> 00:12:03,480
Good if he doesn't.

168
00:12:04,080 --> 00:12:04,799
I'm sick of seeing him.

169
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:05,440
Halt!

170
00:12:09,039 --> 00:12:09,639
Captain Liao. Captain Liao.

171
00:12:17,559 --> 00:12:17,919
What's up?

172
00:12:20,080 --> 00:12:22,279
Let's talk about me joining the SWAT team.

173
00:12:23,960 --> 00:12:25,639
What's there to talk about? The leaders already decided.

174
00:12:25,879 --> 00:12:27,519
Do you really want me on the SWAT team?

175
00:12:28,679 --> 00:12:29,200
No, I don't.

176
00:12:29,279 --> 00:12:30,039
Neither do I.

177
00:12:32,120 --> 00:12:33,120
I have a win-win solution.

178
00:12:37,600 --> 00:12:38,039
Director.

179
00:12:38,200 --> 00:12:38,960
You haven't eaten yet, right?

180
00:12:39,679 --> 00:12:40,399
I just steamed these this morning.

181
00:12:42,000 --> 00:12:42,360
Steamed buns.

182
00:12:43,399 --> 00:12:43,840
What's the filling?

183
00:12:44,360 --> 00:12:45,799
Pork cracklings and glass noodles.

184
00:12:46,879 --> 00:12:47,720
Let's taste your cooking.

185
00:12:52,399 --> 00:12:52,799
Still hot, right?

186
00:12:52,879 --> 00:12:53,399
Yes, it is.

187
00:13:00,840 --> 00:13:01,799
The glass noodles you made

188
00:13:02,159 --> 00:13:02,799
are quite chewy.

189
00:13:03,240 --> 00:13:04,039
I learned it online.

190
00:13:04,720 --> 00:13:05,840
You put a little salt in the water.

191
00:13:11,919 --> 00:13:13,600
And the pork cracklings are exceptionally savory too.

192
00:13:15,039 --> 00:13:15,639
I bought

193
00:13:16,159 --> 00:13:16,679
organic,

194
00:13:17,000 --> 00:13:17,840
free-range pork.

195
00:13:18,159 --> 00:13:18,919
Black pork?

196
00:13:19,879 --> 00:13:20,480
That's way too expensive.

197
00:13:23,159 --> 00:13:23,960
It's worth it for peace of mind.

198
00:13:25,159 --> 00:13:26,879
You used such expensive meat for cracklings?

199
00:13:27,639 --> 00:13:28,240
What a waste.

200
00:13:29,399 --> 00:13:30,639
Not a waste if you're eating it.

201
00:13:34,879 --> 00:13:35,320
You need a favor, don't you?

202
00:13:41,159 --> 00:13:42,120
Just say it.

203
00:13:45,720 --> 00:13:46,320
I just wanted

204
00:13:47,080 --> 00:13:48,080
to talk about

205
00:13:48,200 --> 00:13:49,799
my personal job reassignment.

206
00:13:50,279 --> 00:13:52,440
I have some rough ideas.

207
00:13:53,679 --> 00:13:55,120
If they're rough, then don't share them.

208
00:13:58,919 --> 00:13:59,919
Please, eat first.

209
00:14:04,440 --> 00:14:05,200
I know

210
00:14:06,960 --> 00:14:08,919
you have an issue with Lao Zhao being

211
00:14:09,919 --> 00:14:10,440
the director of the Publicity Department.

212
00:14:11,399 --> 00:14:11,919
No, no, no.

213
00:14:12,480 --> 00:14:13,480
As for the organization's arrangement,

214
00:14:13,639 --> 00:14:14,480
I am in full agreement.

215
00:14:15,159 --> 00:14:16,440
The Publicity Department also needs

216
00:14:16,440 --> 00:14:17,879
a comrade like Zhao Guohua,

217
00:14:17,919 --> 00:14:20,279
an experienced veteran with both seniority and expertise,

218
00:14:20,559 --> 00:14:21,360
to take charge of the work.

219
00:14:22,279 --> 00:14:23,879
I just wanted to discuss with you

220
00:14:24,240 --> 00:14:25,080
if my personal

221
00:14:25,960 --> 00:14:27,679
job reassignment has any other possibilities.

222
00:14:29,919 --> 00:14:30,720
Then you must have

223
00:14:30,720 --> 00:14:31,639
an issue with going to

224
00:14:32,039 --> 00:14:32,600
the SWAT detachment.

225
00:14:36,279 --> 00:14:36,679
Director Guo,

226
00:14:37,000 --> 00:14:37,519
I know

227
00:14:37,519 --> 00:14:40,080
letting me serve as the SWAT detachment's commissar

228
00:14:40,960 --> 00:14:42,320
is entirely due to your

229
00:14:42,879 --> 00:14:43,440
trust in me.

230
00:14:44,559 --> 00:14:45,240
At work,

231
00:14:46,200 --> 00:14:48,080
I have made full preparations.

232
00:14:48,399 --> 00:14:50,000
I even went to the SWAT detachment this morning

233
00:14:50,000 --> 00:14:51,799
to familiarize myself with it in advance.

234
00:14:52,240 --> 00:14:53,000
Isn't that great?

235
00:14:53,600 --> 00:14:54,440
Just do your best.

236
00:14:55,720 --> 00:14:56,919
You can rest assured on that.

237
00:14:58,080 --> 00:14:59,960
Any problems I encounter at work,

238
00:14:59,960 --> 00:15:00,639
I can overcome them.

239
00:15:00,879 --> 00:15:01,600
I'm just afraid...

240
00:15:02,279 --> 00:15:02,879
What are you afraid of?

241
00:15:07,080 --> 00:15:08,919
Because when I was working in the Publicity Department,

242
00:15:09,279 --> 00:15:10,240
the SWAT detachment over there

243
00:15:10,480 --> 00:15:12,000
had some resistance to

244
00:15:12,000 --> 00:15:13,039
some of my work arrangements.

245
00:15:16,080 --> 00:15:17,039
I don't care about that.

246
00:15:17,480 --> 00:15:18,240
I'm worried

247
00:15:18,840 --> 00:15:19,960
their personal opinions of me

248
00:15:19,960 --> 00:15:21,000
might affect the overall work.

249
00:15:22,480 --> 00:15:23,759
If internal problems arise,

250
00:15:24,879 --> 00:15:26,080
it won't be worth it.

251
00:15:27,919 --> 00:15:28,440
So I was wondering

252
00:15:29,159 --> 00:15:31,039
if I could be transferred to another detachment.

253
00:15:37,399 --> 00:15:37,679
Tan Yan,

254
00:15:40,440 --> 00:15:41,879
regarding their opinions and issues with you,

255
00:15:43,000 --> 00:15:45,039
I think they are negligible.

256
00:15:46,159 --> 00:15:46,759
Even if there are any,

257
00:15:46,759 --> 00:15:47,759
as a political cadre,

258
00:15:48,919 --> 00:15:50,480
you have to face and handle them.

259
00:15:52,559 --> 00:15:53,360
The SWAT detachment,

260
00:15:53,759 --> 00:15:54,559
where do its key problems lie?

261
00:15:55,799 --> 00:15:56,879
You should know better than anyone.

262
00:15:57,879 --> 00:15:58,840
Sending you there

263
00:15:59,960 --> 00:16:00,639
is because I want you

264
00:16:00,639 --> 00:16:02,279
to resolve all those problems for me.

265
00:16:04,720 --> 00:16:06,279
The organization sees

266
00:16:07,240 --> 00:16:08,279
the progress you've made.

267
00:16:10,440 --> 00:16:11,639
We have plans for your

268
00:16:12,080 --> 00:16:13,240
future positions.

269
00:16:14,720 --> 00:16:16,399
This is both a sign of trust

270
00:16:17,120 --> 00:16:18,279
and recognition.

271
00:16:27,559 --> 00:16:29,000
If you really don't want to go,

272
00:16:30,080 --> 00:16:30,639
that's fine too.

273
00:16:31,639 --> 00:16:32,799
Our bureau's party organization

274
00:16:33,480 --> 00:16:34,440
can reconsider.

275
00:16:36,399 --> 00:16:37,960
But don't think about other detachments.

276
00:16:38,759 --> 00:16:39,960
You can just stay in the

277
00:16:40,360 --> 00:16:40,919
Publicity Department

278
00:16:41,279 --> 00:16:42,919
and cooperate well with Lao Zhao's work.

279
00:16:44,279 --> 00:16:45,679
I... I have no objections, Director Guo.

280
00:16:45,679 --> 00:16:46,600
You might have misunderstood me.

281
00:16:48,759 --> 00:16:50,879
I was single-handedly trained by you.

282
00:16:50,879 --> 00:16:53,159
How could I let down your expectations of me?

283
00:16:53,600 --> 00:16:54,600
I will definitely do a good job.

284
00:16:54,960 --> 00:16:55,480
Rest assured.

285
00:16:55,879 --> 00:16:56,480
Let's hope so.

286
00:16:57,519 --> 00:16:58,320
I will. Definitely.

287
00:17:04,039 --> 00:17:04,599
Director Yu

288
00:17:06,079 --> 00:17:07,920
will reach retirement age in a few years.

289
00:17:08,599 --> 00:17:09,839
It all depends on your performance.

290
00:17:10,799 --> 00:17:11,880
You need to do well.

291
00:17:13,680 --> 00:17:14,000
Come in.

292
00:17:15,160 --> 00:17:16,279
You also need to perform well.

293
00:17:20,079 --> 00:17:20,599
Why are you here?

294
00:17:27,039 --> 00:17:27,240
Come.

295
00:17:28,799 --> 00:17:29,079
Sit.

296
00:17:29,599 --> 00:17:30,119
Look,

297
00:17:30,640 --> 00:17:31,160
Tan Yan

298
00:17:31,359 --> 00:17:32,119
steamed some buns.

299
00:17:32,319 --> 00:17:33,359
They're stuffed with pork cracklings and glass noodles.

300
00:17:33,920 --> 00:17:34,559
Come try some.

301
00:17:34,839 --> 00:17:35,319
I'm not eating.

302
00:17:38,200 --> 00:17:38,720
What's wrong?

303
00:17:39,400 --> 00:17:41,599
Why such a long face?

304
00:17:41,880 --> 00:17:42,519
Who is it for?

305
00:17:43,599 --> 00:17:44,759
Not for you, Director Guo.

306
00:17:46,319 --> 00:17:46,920
It's for him.

307
00:17:48,519 --> 00:17:50,960
Our SWAT team doesn't need a smooth-talking,

308
00:17:51,559 --> 00:17:52,400
scheming,

309
00:17:53,160 --> 00:17:54,079
glory hound like him.

310
00:17:56,759 --> 00:17:57,640
Haven't seen you for a few days,

311
00:17:58,160 --> 00:17:59,400
and you've learned a lot of new words.

312
00:17:59,880 --> 00:18:00,480
What's the matter?

313
00:18:01,200 --> 00:18:03,240
Do you have a problem with the organization's arrangement too?

314
00:18:03,559 --> 00:18:04,079
I do.

315
00:18:05,799 --> 00:18:06,240
Director Guo.

316
00:18:07,240 --> 00:18:08,440
Commissar Lu just died in the line of duty.

317
00:18:10,119 --> 00:18:11,319
And you're just going to take this

318
00:18:12,039 --> 00:18:13,440
guy who only knows how to write reports

319
00:18:13,440 --> 00:18:14,480
and throw him into our SWAT detachment?

320
00:18:15,160 --> 00:18:15,799
I refuse to accept this.

321
00:18:16,880 --> 00:18:18,400
Wait, you don't accept it?

322
00:18:18,480 --> 00:18:18,720
Well...

323
00:18:18,720 --> 00:18:19,160
Captain Liao, Captain Liao.

324
00:18:19,440 --> 00:18:20,880
If you have a problem with me personally,

325
00:18:20,880 --> 00:18:21,720
you can tell me to my face.

326
00:18:22,680 --> 00:18:24,440
But the organization's arrangement

327
00:18:24,440 --> 00:18:26,240
was made after careful consideration.

328
00:18:26,839 --> 00:18:28,359
Don't make things difficult for the organization.

329
00:18:30,119 --> 00:18:30,640
Director Guo.

330
00:18:31,599 --> 00:18:32,400
Captain Liao has a big problem

331
00:18:33,079 --> 00:18:33,799
with me.

332
00:18:35,000 --> 00:18:36,160
I'm well aware

333
00:18:37,480 --> 00:18:39,599
of the difficulties I'll face

334
00:18:39,759 --> 00:18:41,119
as the future SWAT commissar.

335
00:18:41,519 --> 00:18:42,960
But I have the resolve and confidence

336
00:18:43,960 --> 00:18:45,799
to complete the task the organization has given me.

337
00:18:50,359 --> 00:18:51,039
Deputy Director Tan.

338
00:18:51,799 --> 00:18:52,759
This morning at the SWAT unit,

339
00:18:52,759 --> 00:18:54,079
that's not what you told me.

340
00:18:58,920 --> 00:19:00,680
True, I did say this morning

341
00:19:00,680 --> 00:19:01,880
that I didn't want to go to the SWAT detachment.

342
00:19:02,200 --> 00:19:04,079
And you also made it clear you didn't want me there.

343
00:19:04,319 --> 00:19:04,720
Right.

344
00:19:05,319 --> 00:19:07,160
But on my way back,

345
00:19:08,000 --> 00:19:08,920
I reflected a lot.

346
00:19:10,640 --> 00:19:11,759
And analyzed a lot.

347
00:19:13,160 --> 00:19:14,319
No matter who it is,

348
00:19:15,160 --> 00:19:17,000
one shouldn't put their personal wishes

349
00:19:17,000 --> 00:19:18,920
above the organization's arrangements.

350
00:19:19,480 --> 00:19:20,440
The organization's decision,

351
00:19:21,279 --> 00:19:22,920
I accept unconditionally.

352
00:19:26,119 --> 00:19:28,599
I also hope that in our future work,

353
00:19:28,880 --> 00:19:29,759
if there are difficulties,

354
00:19:30,359 --> 00:19:31,160
we overcome them together.

355
00:19:31,279 --> 00:19:32,000
If there are problems,

356
00:19:32,279 --> 00:19:33,119
we solve them together.

357
00:19:33,279 --> 00:19:34,559
Together, we'll forge the SWAT detachment

358
00:19:34,680 --> 00:19:36,920
into the Hongye Public Security system's

359
00:19:37,960 --> 00:19:38,920
sharpest blade.

360
00:19:44,960 --> 00:19:46,319
Didn't he just make his stance clear?

361
00:19:53,880 --> 00:19:54,880
Work hand in hand.

362
00:19:58,359 --> 00:19:58,720
Fine.

363
00:20:20,920 --> 00:20:21,599
Have a seat.

364
00:20:22,880 --> 00:20:23,799
Director Guo, I'm fine now.

365
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:25,000
Then I'm fine too, Director Guo.

366
00:20:27,519 --> 00:20:28,839
I'll wash the container and return it.

367
00:20:29,599 --> 00:20:30,359
I'll clean it up.

368
00:20:40,839 --> 00:20:41,680
None of them make it easy.

369
00:20:54,519 --> 00:20:55,240
Lv Xiao!

370
00:20:55,839 --> 00:20:56,279
Here!

371
00:20:56,720 --> 00:20:57,400
What are you doing?

372
00:20:57,519 --> 00:20:58,519
Can't even hold your handcuffs?

373
00:20:58,920 --> 00:21:00,279
Your squad, 100 push-ups.

374
00:21:00,440 --> 00:21:00,759
Yes, sir!

375
00:21:00,960 --> 00:21:01,799
The rest of you, take a break.

376
00:21:07,039 --> 00:21:08,839
I mean, did he have to be so strict?

377
00:21:10,839 --> 00:21:12,079
Anyone can tell today

378
00:21:12,279 --> 00:21:13,319
Captain Liao is in a bad mood.

379
00:21:13,799 --> 00:21:15,200
You just had to step right into the line of fire.

380
00:21:15,599 --> 00:21:17,240
And now you've got us all punished too.

381
00:21:18,000 --> 00:21:18,759
Dinner's on me tonight.

382
00:21:21,440 --> 00:21:21,799
Captain Liao.

383
00:21:22,319 --> 00:21:23,240
Someone from the Political Department is here for you.

384
00:21:31,440 --> 00:21:33,200
This transfer order was approved a while ago.

385
00:21:33,440 --> 00:21:34,599
Director Yu held onto it for a few days.

386
00:21:34,759 --> 00:21:35,839
He specifically told me

387
00:21:36,119 --> 00:21:37,000
to wait until after the memorial service

388
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:38,039
before bringing it over to you.

389
00:22:05,160 --> 00:22:05,920
Fall in!

390
00:22:14,720 --> 00:22:15,160
Stand at ease.

391
00:22:25,079 --> 00:22:26,480
I received a transfer order.

392
00:22:29,440 --> 00:22:30,720
One of our comrades

393
00:22:31,559 --> 00:22:33,079
will be leaving our SWAT team.

394
00:22:40,640 --> 00:22:41,119
Wang Yunsheng!

395
00:22:41,440 --> 00:22:41,680
Here!

396
00:22:42,079 --> 00:22:42,440
Step forward.

397
00:22:42,759 --> 00:22:43,039
Yes, sir.

398
00:22:50,599 --> 00:22:51,440
Wang Yunsheng!

399
00:22:52,079 --> 00:22:52,839
What's the meaning of this?

400
00:22:54,880 --> 00:22:56,240
Commissar Lu just passed away and you're bailing,

401
00:22:57,160 --> 00:22:57,880
just to spite us?

402
00:23:03,880 --> 00:23:04,240
What are you doing?

403
00:23:14,480 --> 00:23:14,880
Captain Liao...

404
00:23:16,039 --> 00:23:17,119
I actually didn't want to leave right now.

405
00:23:17,279 --> 00:23:18,000
Everyone has their own ambitions.

406
00:23:20,039 --> 00:23:20,839
Your career...

407
00:23:21,640 --> 00:23:22,480
we won't stand in your way.

408
00:23:23,799 --> 00:23:24,319
Right?

409
00:23:25,599 --> 00:23:26,160
Yes, sir.

410
00:23:26,279 --> 00:23:26,960
Louder!

411
00:23:27,119 --> 00:23:27,839
Yes, sir!

412
00:23:39,319 --> 00:23:40,079
What's the rush?

413
00:23:57,119 --> 00:23:57,640
Attention, everyone!

414
00:24:21,640 --> 00:24:22,240
Salute!

415
00:24:46,079 --> 00:24:47,960
Is the SWAT team really this easy to push around?

416
00:24:48,400 --> 00:24:49,599
Commissar Lu just died in the line of duty,

417
00:24:49,640 --> 00:24:50,519
and they already transferred someone out.

418
00:24:51,200 --> 00:24:51,799
What do we do now?

419
00:24:52,400 --> 00:24:53,519
First time seeing someone off?

420
00:24:54,279 --> 00:24:55,079
Just get back to work.

421
00:25:11,680 --> 00:25:13,839
We really can't blame anyone else for this.

422
00:25:14,359 --> 00:25:16,160
It's just that we can't retain people here.

423
00:25:19,359 --> 00:25:20,000
For major cases,

424
00:25:20,880 --> 00:25:21,440
we only play a supporting role.

425
00:25:22,400 --> 00:25:23,400
We're number one in danger,

426
00:25:24,519 --> 00:25:26,240
but always dead last in credit.

427
00:25:27,880 --> 00:25:28,559
Earning merits here

428
00:25:29,319 --> 00:25:30,240
is harder than at a local station.

429
00:25:32,799 --> 00:25:33,240
So, Master,

430
00:25:33,839 --> 00:25:35,720
is that why you transferred to Traffic?

431
00:25:44,119 --> 00:25:44,559
Yes.

432
00:25:45,799 --> 00:25:46,359
And no.

433
00:25:47,759 --> 00:25:48,640
At least I'm an officer.

434
00:25:49,640 --> 00:25:50,160
But what about Yunsheng?

435
00:25:51,079 --> 00:25:52,200
He doesn't even have an official staff position.

436
00:25:54,799 --> 00:25:56,960
He just wants to earn merits quickly

437
00:25:57,160 --> 00:25:57,920
and become a regular cop.

438
00:25:58,960 --> 00:26:00,200
Why can't you understand that?

439
00:26:00,759 --> 00:26:01,720
Why are you giving him a hard time?

440
00:26:03,319 --> 00:26:04,799
So where did he get transferred?

441
00:26:06,240 --> 00:26:06,960
Gurong Station.

442
00:26:08,799 --> 00:26:09,160
Wait.

443
00:26:09,880 --> 00:26:11,319
Doesn't Director Tan's wife work at Gurong?

444
00:26:11,880 --> 00:26:13,200
Is that snake Tan Yan pulling strings

445
00:26:13,200 --> 00:26:13,759
to get him transferred?

446
00:26:19,440 --> 00:26:20,400
Watch your mouth.

447
00:26:21,680 --> 00:26:22,599
Show some respect.

448
00:26:22,920 --> 00:26:23,960
Who are you calling a snake?

449
00:26:25,440 --> 00:26:26,559
He's about to become our

450
00:26:27,039 --> 00:26:27,440
Commissar.

451
00:26:29,359 --> 00:26:30,400
You idiot.

452
00:26:34,359 --> 00:26:35,559
Tan Yan or whoever he is,

453
00:26:36,000 --> 00:26:36,640
I refuse to accept him.

454
00:26:38,440 --> 00:26:38,799
Do you?

455
00:26:39,920 --> 00:26:40,440
What choice do we have?

456
00:26:45,880 --> 00:26:46,559
Commissar Tan.

457
00:26:50,279 --> 00:26:50,680
Director Tan.

458
00:26:51,079 --> 00:26:51,480
Director Tan.

459
00:27:02,759 --> 00:27:03,680
Director Tan, let me handle it. Let me.

460
00:27:03,880 --> 00:27:04,519
Let me handle it.

461
00:27:07,920 --> 00:27:09,079
Director Zhao, where should this plant go?

462
00:27:09,799 --> 00:27:11,079
Quick, give it to me. Give it here.

463
00:27:11,079 --> 00:27:12,200
Just tell me where. Just tell me.

464
00:27:12,720 --> 00:27:13,119
Here, here.

465
00:27:13,839 --> 00:27:14,240
Put it here.

466
00:27:14,240 --> 00:27:14,519
Director Tan.

467
00:27:16,799 --> 00:27:17,680
This is perfect. It's perfect.

468
00:27:19,440 --> 00:27:19,799
Director Tan.

469
00:27:21,680 --> 00:27:22,519
About this appointment,

470
00:27:22,759 --> 00:27:24,000
I didn't expect it at all.

471
00:27:24,920 --> 00:27:26,400
But in terms of professional ability,

472
00:27:26,920 --> 00:27:28,039
you're actually more suitable than I am.

473
00:27:28,440 --> 00:27:29,680
Don't say that. Don't say that, Director Zhao.

474
00:27:30,440 --> 00:27:32,640
The Publicity Department needs veterans like you

475
00:27:32,920 --> 00:27:33,799
at the helm.

476
00:27:34,119 --> 00:27:35,039
The organization's arrangement

477
00:27:35,440 --> 00:27:36,680
is very wise.

478
00:27:38,359 --> 00:27:39,759
Let's see what else I can help you move.

479
00:27:39,759 --> 00:27:40,400
No need, nothing else.

480
00:27:40,400 --> 00:27:40,920
It's all moved. All moved.

481
00:27:41,000 --> 00:27:42,000
Xiao Qu, are we done moving?

482
00:27:42,519 --> 00:27:43,000
Yes, we're done.

483
00:27:44,720 --> 00:27:45,839
The sunlight here is great, right?

484
00:27:45,839 --> 00:27:47,039
The view is nice too.

485
00:27:51,480 --> 00:27:51,839
Director Zhao.

486
00:27:53,240 --> 00:27:53,599
I'm leaving this for you.

487
00:27:54,799 --> 00:27:56,400
It's that really good tea from last time.

488
00:27:56,759 --> 00:27:57,759
Take it. Take it.

489
00:27:58,039 --> 00:27:59,400
I've been drinking your tea all these years.

490
00:28:01,000 --> 00:28:01,680
I won't drink this box.

491
00:28:02,039 --> 00:28:02,799
I'll keep it as a memento.

492
00:28:02,839 --> 00:28:03,400
You have to drink it.

493
00:28:03,480 --> 00:28:04,519
When you run out, I'll get you more.

494
00:28:05,839 --> 00:28:06,960
Don't be polite with me.

495
00:28:09,640 --> 00:28:10,559
I'm a little reluctant to leave.

496
00:28:11,400 --> 00:28:13,000
I'm heading to the SWAT detachment soon.

497
00:28:14,720 --> 00:28:16,079
For our future publicity work over there,

498
00:28:16,079 --> 00:28:17,079
please give it some thought.

499
00:28:17,759 --> 00:28:18,519
Stop joking.

500
00:28:19,039 --> 00:28:20,920
As if you need me to worry about publicity.

501
00:28:20,920 --> 00:28:21,920
Of course I do.

502
00:28:22,799 --> 00:28:23,680
Whatever you need,

503
00:28:23,680 --> 00:28:24,720
just tell me anytime.

504
00:28:24,799 --> 00:28:26,440
The Publicity Department will fully cooperate with Director Tan.

505
00:28:26,519 --> 00:28:27,680
Then I won't hesitate.

506
00:28:27,920 --> 00:28:28,279
Wait, no.

507
00:28:29,559 --> 00:28:29,920
Commissar Tan.

508
00:28:36,720 --> 00:28:37,839
Director Zhao, where did you get these cardboard boxes?

509
00:28:38,200 --> 00:28:39,839
I need a couple to move my stuff too.

510
00:28:40,519 --> 00:28:40,839
Do you have any?

511
00:28:41,559 --> 00:28:41,920
Xiao Qu.

512
00:28:42,960 --> 00:28:43,319
Logistics.

513
00:28:43,599 --> 00:28:44,559
Is one enough?

514
00:28:44,559 --> 00:28:45,319
Two, I guess.

515
00:28:45,319 --> 00:28:45,680
Three.

516
00:28:46,200 --> 00:28:46,680
Get three.

517
00:28:46,960 --> 00:28:47,279
Cardboard boxes.

518
00:28:51,400 --> 00:28:52,400
See you at the courtyard tonight.

519
00:29:02,680 --> 00:29:04,759
Lao Tan, what are we having today?

520
00:29:05,240 --> 00:29:05,759
Order whatever.

521
00:29:06,920 --> 00:29:07,440
It's on me.

522
00:29:08,480 --> 00:29:09,000
I don't care.

523
00:29:09,680 --> 00:29:10,160
I don't care about the cost.

524
00:29:15,359 --> 00:29:16,319
Stop acting like a big shot.

525
00:29:19,000 --> 00:29:20,160
You don't care about this, you don't care about that.

526
00:29:21,960 --> 00:29:22,920
You might not care, but I do.

527
00:29:23,880 --> 00:29:24,680
What else don't you care about?

528
00:29:26,160 --> 00:29:27,240
Fine, care all you want.

529
00:29:28,480 --> 00:29:29,839
Seriously, why are you being so passive-aggressive?

530
00:29:30,799 --> 00:29:31,759
I just said I'm treating.

531
00:29:31,759 --> 00:29:33,240
I said I don't care about the cost of food.

532
00:29:34,920 --> 00:29:35,599
And you're making a fuss.

533
00:29:45,720 --> 00:29:46,720
That's how it is.

534
00:29:48,680 --> 00:29:49,319
If you ask me,

535
00:29:49,319 --> 00:29:50,200
an officer,

536
00:29:51,640 --> 00:29:54,160
with firm ideals and convictions,

537
00:29:54,960 --> 00:29:56,160
will be able to stand strong

538
00:29:58,119 --> 00:30:00,240
against winds from all directions,

539
00:30:01,400 --> 00:30:04,279
and remain steady as a mountain.

540
00:30:06,400 --> 00:30:07,720
I still need to temper myself.

541
00:30:10,400 --> 00:30:12,880
This is a great opportunity for me to grow.

542
00:30:24,440 --> 00:30:25,200
I can't keep this up.

543
00:30:28,039 --> 00:30:29,759
Actually, I have it all figured out.

544
00:30:30,319 --> 00:30:32,000
I'll just do this for two years,

545
00:30:32,200 --> 00:30:33,359
then head back to headquarters.

546
00:30:33,960 --> 00:30:35,960
They'll make arrangements for me.

547
00:30:37,920 --> 00:30:38,759
What arrangements?

548
00:30:41,480 --> 00:30:42,279
What arrangements?

549
00:30:43,200 --> 00:30:44,480
What kind of arrangements?

550
00:30:46,720 --> 00:30:48,000
I won't have to return to the Publicity Department.

551
00:30:48,119 --> 00:30:49,160
The Publicity Department?

552
00:30:49,960 --> 00:30:51,440
You need to think bigger.

553
00:30:51,720 --> 00:30:53,279
Come on, enlighten us.

554
00:30:53,920 --> 00:30:55,759
You're just feeding yourself a pipe dream.

555
00:30:55,759 --> 00:30:57,599
Feeding yourself a pipe dream.

556
00:30:57,759 --> 00:30:59,319
It's not a pipe dream.

557
00:31:04,319 --> 00:31:05,000
You believe that?

558
00:31:05,480 --> 00:31:06,079
I do.

559
00:31:08,079 --> 00:31:08,759
You really believe that?

560
00:31:09,480 --> 00:31:10,480
I really do.

561
00:31:12,599 --> 00:31:13,319
Believe what you want.

562
00:31:13,319 --> 00:31:13,920
I don't believe it.

563
00:31:28,839 --> 00:31:29,880
You guys have an occupational disease.

564
00:31:31,920 --> 00:31:32,880
You just love suspecting people.

565
00:31:33,599 --> 00:31:35,000
Old Guo and I go way back.

566
00:31:35,359 --> 00:31:37,599
There are some things I just can't tell you outright.

567
00:31:38,720 --> 00:31:39,119
You're here.

568
00:31:39,480 --> 00:31:40,039
Have a seat.

569
00:31:40,359 --> 00:31:42,200
I was about to leave when two people came in arguing.

570
00:31:44,759 --> 00:31:45,119
What's going on?

571
00:31:45,759 --> 00:31:46,079
Lin Nan.

572
00:31:48,000 --> 00:31:48,519
It's nothing.

573
00:31:49,680 --> 00:31:50,880
He's just feeding himself pipe dreams.

574
00:31:51,680 --> 00:31:53,000
No, I'm not.

575
00:31:53,759 --> 00:31:54,480
What's the occasion today?

576
00:31:54,480 --> 00:31:55,720
I have good news for you.

577
00:31:56,880 --> 00:31:57,559
What good news?

578
00:31:58,240 --> 00:32:00,319
Bouncing back from rock bottom. A roundabout victory.

579
00:32:00,720 --> 00:32:01,319
It worked?

580
00:32:09,519 --> 00:32:11,400
Didn't steam those buns all night for nothing.

581
00:32:12,759 --> 00:32:13,640
The food is here!

582
00:32:14,319 --> 00:32:15,000
Chief Ji is here.

583
00:32:16,039 --> 00:32:17,440
Come on, give me a hand.

584
00:32:17,440 --> 00:32:18,119
Let's serve the cold dishes first.

585
00:32:18,119 --> 00:32:18,279
Here.

586
00:32:19,440 --> 00:32:20,000
Alright.

587
00:32:21,400 --> 00:32:22,119
Let's start drinking.

588
00:32:24,720 --> 00:32:26,319
Those who didn't report in, drink tea instead of alcohol.

589
00:32:35,160 --> 00:32:35,640
You drink tea.

590
00:32:36,640 --> 00:32:36,960
Okay.

591
00:32:38,039 --> 00:32:39,839
Then let's toast to me, Lao Tan, first.

592
00:32:41,240 --> 00:32:42,039
For dropping the "Deputy" title.

593
00:32:42,039 --> 00:32:43,480
Promoted to Political Commissar of the SWAT Detachment.

594
00:32:55,599 --> 00:32:57,079
Remember what we said back then,

595
00:32:57,079 --> 00:32:58,799
over drinks after college graduation?

596
00:33:10,960 --> 00:33:12,440
I don't seek wealth or glory,

597
00:33:17,720 --> 00:33:20,559
just a clear conscience.

598
00:34:16,679 --> 00:34:17,639
You must be Commissar Tan.

599
00:34:22,960 --> 00:34:23,480
Commissar Tan.

600
00:34:24,760 --> 00:34:25,679
Welcome to the SWAT team.

601
00:34:28,440 --> 00:34:30,719
I'm the assault team captain, Liu Lang.

602
00:34:30,960 --> 00:34:31,599
Hello, Liu Lang.

603
00:34:32,079 --> 00:34:32,719
Hello, hello.

604
00:34:34,119 --> 00:34:35,639
Is it your day off today?

605
00:34:35,840 --> 00:34:36,320
No.

606
00:34:37,119 --> 00:34:37,800
Where is everyone else?

607
00:34:39,000 --> 00:34:39,519
Well...

608
00:34:39,920 --> 00:34:40,960
Captain Liao took the team out

609
00:34:41,239 --> 00:34:42,119
for training early this morning.

610
00:34:42,440 --> 00:34:43,760
He specifically asked me to stay behind

611
00:34:43,920 --> 00:34:44,559
to welcome you.

612
00:34:47,400 --> 00:34:48,320
How about we

613
00:34:48,840 --> 00:34:49,719
check out the honors room?

614
00:34:53,119 --> 00:34:53,559
Commissar Tan,

615
00:34:54,280 --> 00:34:55,079
our SWAT team

616
00:34:55,440 --> 00:34:56,559
is different from other police units.

617
00:34:57,599 --> 00:34:58,679
We do minor drills every day,

618
00:34:59,079 --> 00:35:00,119
and major drills every three days.

619
00:35:06,280 --> 00:35:06,639
Mind the stairs.

620
00:35:11,280 --> 00:35:11,760
Commissar,

621
00:35:12,679 --> 00:35:13,159
right this way.

622
00:35:15,679 --> 00:35:17,039
This is our honors room.

623
00:35:17,719 --> 00:35:19,639
We also use it as a reception room.

624
00:35:20,719 --> 00:35:21,559
Since the team was founded,

625
00:35:21,880 --> 00:35:22,880
all the honors we've received

626
00:35:23,400 --> 00:35:24,440
are displayed right here.

627
00:35:27,320 --> 00:35:27,559
Right.

628
00:35:29,760 --> 00:35:30,519
Come, have a seat first.

629
00:35:31,039 --> 00:35:32,320
Captain Liao and the others should be back soon.

630
00:35:38,239 --> 00:35:38,440
By the way,

631
00:35:38,960 --> 00:35:39,239
Commissar,

632
00:35:39,760 --> 00:35:40,639
do you usually prefer tea

633
00:35:40,639 --> 00:35:41,400
or coffee?

634
00:35:42,079 --> 00:35:42,639
Coffee, I guess.

635
00:35:44,199 --> 00:35:44,559
We don't have any.

636
00:35:45,480 --> 00:35:46,119
Tea is fine too.

637
00:35:48,000 --> 00:35:48,639
We don't have that either.

638
00:35:52,519 --> 00:35:53,920
I'm just trying to learn

639
00:35:53,920 --> 00:35:54,719
my superior's preferences in advance.

640
00:35:56,039 --> 00:35:57,079
I'll make sure to stock up on them later.

641
00:35:58,000 --> 00:35:59,800
Conditions here at the SWAT team are pretty rough.

642
00:36:00,199 --> 00:36:01,679
Forget about tea and coffee,

643
00:36:02,239 --> 00:36:03,719
we don't even have enough bottled water.

644
00:36:06,480 --> 00:36:07,079
You have boiled water, right?

645
00:36:07,639 --> 00:36:08,360
We do have boiled water.

646
00:36:13,800 --> 00:36:14,679
Oh, I just remembered,

647
00:36:15,559 --> 00:36:16,679
the water dispenser is broken too.

648
00:36:17,280 --> 00:36:19,039
Tell you what, I'll go boil a pot for you right now.

649
00:37:06,920 --> 00:37:07,719
Sorry to keep you waiting.

650
00:37:08,400 --> 00:37:08,960
Here's your boiled water.

651
00:37:09,440 --> 00:37:09,840
Captain Liu.

652
00:37:10,119 --> 00:37:12,199
This little thing in the honors room...

653
00:37:12,199 --> 00:37:13,000
Is there a story behind it?

654
00:37:21,440 --> 00:37:22,000
What's this?

655
00:37:22,880 --> 00:37:23,280
Where did it come from?

656
00:37:24,360 --> 00:37:25,280
It was sitting right here.

657
00:37:26,039 --> 00:37:26,599
Never seen it before.

658
00:37:28,519 --> 00:37:29,199
Never seen it.

659
00:37:35,199 --> 00:37:35,920
Interesting.

660
00:37:44,000 --> 00:37:44,639
Hurry up and go upstairs.

661
00:37:44,639 --> 00:37:45,519
He's been waiting ages for you.

662
00:37:46,320 --> 00:37:46,840
Why is he waiting for me?

663
00:37:48,599 --> 00:37:50,519
Just take him to his office to start work.

664
00:37:51,320 --> 00:37:52,320
That's not appropriate, is it?

665
00:37:54,360 --> 00:37:55,480
He's newly appointed.

666
00:37:56,320 --> 00:37:57,599
As the detachment captain,

667
00:37:57,800 --> 00:37:59,079
how can you not even say hello?

668
00:37:59,719 --> 00:38:00,400
There's no need.

669
00:38:02,519 --> 00:38:03,119
What do you mean, there's no...

670
00:38:04,000 --> 00:38:04,280
You're...

671
00:38:14,119 --> 00:38:16,079
Master, is the new commissar here?

672
00:38:17,880 --> 00:38:18,960
Isn't he standing right over there?

673
00:38:19,639 --> 00:38:20,000
Don't look.

674
00:38:23,039 --> 00:38:24,039
That little thing on the desk...

675
00:38:24,039 --> 00:38:24,599
did he see it?

676
00:38:28,440 --> 00:38:29,239
You put that there?

677
00:38:31,159 --> 00:38:32,480
You really have too much free time.

678
00:38:32,639 --> 00:38:33,880
I had to show him who's boss.

679
00:38:34,440 --> 00:38:35,559
He must be furious, right?

680
00:38:36,679 --> 00:38:37,239
No.

681
00:38:38,320 --> 00:38:39,440
He said it was quite interesting.

682
00:38:46,000 --> 00:38:46,360
No way.

683
00:38:47,239 --> 00:38:48,480
I have to put him in his place.

684
00:39:01,199 --> 00:39:01,760
Hello, Commissar.

685
00:39:02,000 --> 00:39:03,119
I'm assault team member Lv Xiao.

686
00:39:03,280 --> 00:39:04,119
Welcome, Commissar Lu.

687
00:39:05,400 --> 00:39:06,159
My last name is Tan.

688
00:39:07,079 --> 00:39:07,719
My name is Tan Yan.

689
00:39:08,920 --> 00:39:09,760
Sorry about that, Commissar Tan.

690
00:39:10,079 --> 00:39:10,559
Force of habit.

691
00:39:12,760 --> 00:39:13,440
You look...

692
00:39:13,440 --> 00:39:14,679
...compared to our Commissar Lu...

693
00:39:14,920 --> 00:39:15,679
...much more composed.

694
00:39:19,039 --> 00:39:20,760
Do you train like this every day?

695
00:39:22,239 --> 00:39:22,559
Yeah.

696
00:39:23,159 --> 00:39:24,599
When Commissar Lu was around,

697
00:39:24,719 --> 00:39:25,679
he'd always tell us

698
00:39:26,159 --> 00:39:28,320
our team is the sharp blade of Hongye.

699
00:39:28,639 --> 00:39:30,199
It needs daily sharpening to keep its edge.

700
00:39:30,519 --> 00:39:31,119
Commissar Lu said

701
00:39:31,559 --> 00:39:32,039
we SWAT officers

702
00:39:32,480 --> 00:39:34,239
must always stay in top condition.

703
00:39:34,920 --> 00:39:35,519
Commissar Lu also said...

704
00:39:35,519 --> 00:39:36,480
Commissar Lu's words...

705
00:39:36,960 --> 00:39:38,280
...you've really taken to heart.

706
00:39:38,800 --> 00:39:39,360
Very good.

707
00:39:43,400 --> 00:39:44,159
As your commissar,

708
00:39:45,360 --> 00:39:46,639
we should talk more from now on.

709
00:39:47,239 --> 00:39:49,239
Whether it's about life or your mindset,

710
00:39:50,320 --> 00:39:51,159
feel free to tell me anytime.

711
00:39:53,119 --> 00:39:53,480
Xiao Li.

712
00:39:59,000 --> 00:39:59,679
Reporting to Commissar Tan,

713
00:40:00,440 --> 00:40:02,159
my last name is Lv. The double-mouth Lv.

714
00:40:08,280 --> 00:40:08,920
I'll let you get to it.

715
00:40:09,519 --> 00:40:10,039
I'm going to change.

716
00:40:26,519 --> 00:40:26,960
Director Guo.

717
00:40:28,039 --> 00:40:28,760
What brings you here?

718
00:40:29,280 --> 00:40:30,159
I had a meeting in the city.

719
00:40:30,480 --> 00:40:31,320
Thought I'd drop by on my way.

720
00:40:32,280 --> 00:40:33,280
What's that you're holding?

721
00:40:35,199 --> 00:40:36,199
A little welcome gift for me.

722
00:40:39,480 --> 00:40:40,000
Where's Liao Bufan?

723
00:40:40,559 --> 00:40:40,920
He's here.

724
00:40:43,239 --> 00:40:43,719
Liao Bufan!

725
00:40:48,760 --> 00:40:49,239
Assemble the team.

726
00:40:49,760 --> 00:40:50,280
Yes, Director Guo.

727
00:41:11,239 --> 00:41:11,800
Salute!

728
00:41:17,440 --> 00:41:17,840
Attention!

729
00:41:21,880 --> 00:41:22,280
Comrades.

730
00:41:24,760 --> 00:41:25,800
The Hongye City

731
00:41:26,360 --> 00:41:27,599
Public Security Bureau Party Committee has decided

732
00:41:28,719 --> 00:41:29,199
to appoint

733
00:41:30,079 --> 00:41:30,880
Comrade Tan Yan

734
00:41:31,840 --> 00:41:32,280
to serve as

735
00:41:33,039 --> 00:41:33,960
the SWAT detachment's

736
00:41:34,440 --> 00:41:35,159
Political Commissar.

737
00:41:36,239 --> 00:41:37,039
Comrade Tan Yan

738
00:41:37,119 --> 00:41:38,079
is no stranger to you all.

739
00:41:38,880 --> 00:41:41,000
Now that he's the new SWAT Commissar,

740
00:41:41,800 --> 00:41:43,400
we hope that in this new role

741
00:41:44,000 --> 00:41:44,880
and new environment,

742
00:41:45,800 --> 00:41:46,480
he'll lead you all

743
00:41:47,199 --> 00:41:48,079
to keep forging ahead

744
00:41:48,840 --> 00:41:49,800
and achieve new breakthroughs.

745
00:41:59,320 --> 00:41:59,880
Commissar Tan,

746
00:42:02,760 --> 00:42:03,599
say a few words to the team.

747
00:42:10,719 --> 00:42:11,000
Come on up.

748
00:42:25,119 --> 00:42:25,639
Hello, comrades.

749
00:42:26,440 --> 00:42:27,039
My name is Tan Yan.

750
00:42:31,519 --> 00:42:31,960
Loyalty,

751
00:42:33,719 --> 00:42:34,239
duty,

752
00:42:34,760 --> 00:42:35,119
courage,

753
00:42:35,760 --> 00:42:36,239
and devotion.

754
00:42:37,559 --> 00:42:40,000
These are what our Hongye SWAT Detachment

755
00:42:40,000 --> 00:42:41,159
since its establishment

756
00:42:41,440 --> 00:42:42,000
has always

757
00:42:42,199 --> 00:42:43,880
upheld as its fine traditions.

758
00:42:46,599 --> 00:42:48,719
I will integrate into your ranks as soon as possible,

759
00:42:49,280 --> 00:42:49,880
and learn to

760
00:42:50,480 --> 00:42:52,119
forge this same tough discipline.

761
00:42:53,519 --> 00:42:55,199
Before coming here, I did some research

762
00:42:56,079 --> 00:42:57,599
and learned that our SWAT Detachment's

763
00:42:58,079 --> 00:43:00,239
ranking in political work

764
00:43:01,079 --> 00:43:01,800
is less than ideal.

765
00:43:12,320 --> 00:43:13,280
As the Commissar,

766
00:43:13,280 --> 00:43:14,559
the political work

767
00:43:14,559 --> 00:43:15,639
is something I'll definitely stay on top of.

768
00:43:15,639 --> 00:43:17,400
Now that you're suddenly free, will you

769
00:43:17,400 --> 00:43:18,599
find it hard to adjust?

770
00:43:18,599 --> 00:43:20,400
The SWAT team only respects the strong.

771
00:43:20,400 --> 00:43:21,519
The SWAT detachment's

772
00:43:21,519 --> 00:43:23,360
personnel turnover issue

773
00:43:23,599 --> 00:43:24,199
is very serious.

774
00:43:24,599 --> 00:43:25,719
Are you afraid

775
00:43:25,719 --> 00:43:27,440
people will think we planned this?

776
00:43:27,920 --> 00:43:28,599
Wang Yunsheng!

777
00:43:28,599 --> 00:43:29,119
Here!

778
00:43:29,840 --> 00:43:31,079
At least we've solved

779
00:43:31,079 --> 00:43:32,880
this immediate talent drain issue.

780
00:43:33,079 --> 00:43:34,360
As long as he's physically in the SWAT team,

781
00:43:34,360 --> 00:43:35,880
do you really think his heart won't follow?
